WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:05.151
August brought several changes and surprises to Aunt Polly's house.

2
00:00:05.152 --> 00:00:15.651
One day, as Pollyanna was walking down the road, she found a kitten.

3
00:00:15.652 --> 00:00:20.492
She went door to door, trying to find the kitten's owner.

4
00:00:20.493 --> 00:00:27.216
When no one claimed it, she brought it home to Aunt Polly, who was reading in the sitting room.

5
00:00:27.217 --> 00:00:33.535
"I was glad I didn't find the owner because I wanted to keep it," Pollyanna confessed.

6
00:00:33.536 --> 00:00:40.698
Aunt Polly stared in horror at the neglected animal Pollyanna was cradling in her arms.

7
00:00:40.699 --> 00:00:45.292
She wasn't fond of cats, not even clean, healthy ones.

8
00:00:45.293 --> 00:00:54.251
"What a dirty beast! I'm sure it's sick and covered with fleas."

9
00:00:54.252 --> 00:00:59.218
"I know." Pollyanna looked tenderly down at the kitten.

10
00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:03.053
"The poor thing doesn't understand we're going to keep it."

11
00:01:03.054 --> 00:01:08.264
"What?" Aunt Polly dropped her book, startling the kitten.

12
00:01:08.265 --> 00:01:15.846
"I told everybody you'd let me keep it if I couldn't find its owner. Poor, lonely little thing."

13
00:01:15.847 --> 00:01:22.297
Aunt Polly tried to speak, but once again she had that strange helpless feeling.

14
00:01:22.298 --> 00:01:28.656
"You took me in, so I knew you wouldn't let this kitty hunt for a home," Pollyanna said.

15
00:01:28.657 --> 00:01:35.083
"At least I had the Ladies' Aid out West, but the poor kitty has no one."

16
00:01:35.084 --> 00:01:37.391
Pollyanna ran happily from the room.

17
00:01:37.392 --> 00:01:41.642
"Pollyanna! Pollyanna! I never said—"

18
00:01:41.643 --> 00:01:45.147
But Pollyanna was already halfway to the kitchen.

19
00:01:45.148 --> 00:01:53.802
"Nancy! Come see this sweet kitty that Aunt Polly's letting me keep! I'm naming her Fluffy!"

20
00:01:53.803 --> 00:01:59.483
Aunt Polly gasped with dismay, but she felt powerless to object.

21
00:01:59.484 --> 00:02:06.220
The next day Pollyanna brought home a dog, even dirtier and more forlorn than the kitten.

22
00:02:06.221 --> 00:02:12.379
Once again Aunt Polly—who disliked dogs even more than cats—said nothing.

23
00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:18.797
How could she protest when Pollyanna saw her as an angel of mercy?

24
00:02:18.798 --> 00:02:23.953
A few days later, Pollyanna found yet another creature for Aunt Polly to take in.

25
00:02:23.954 --> 00:02:32.605
That morning Aunt Polly gave Pollyanna a break from sewing, so Pollyanna visited Mrs. Snow.

26
00:02:32.606 --> 00:02:39.017
The two had become good friends and often played the Glad Game together.

27
00:02:39.018 --> 00:02:45.518
On the way home, Pollyanna spotted a boy sitting by the road, whittling a stick.

28
00:02:45.519 --> 00:02:49.128
"Hello!" Pollyanna said cheerfully.

29
00:02:49.129 --> 00:02:54.821
The boy glanced up but quickly looked away. "Hello yourself."

30
00:02:54.822 --> 00:02:59.811
Although Pollyanna liked adults, she really wanted a friend her own age.

31
00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:03.963
So she was determined to make the most of this opportunity.

32
00:03:03.964 --> 00:03:07.117
"My name's Pollyanna Whittier."

33
00:03:07.118 --> 00:03:12.253
She plopped onto the grass near the boy. "What's yours?"

34
00:03:12.254 --> 00:03:14.301
"Jimmy Bean."

35
00:03:14.302 --> 00:03:16.158
"Where do you live?"

36
00:03:16.159 --> 00:03:18.453
"Nowhere."

37
00:03:18.454 --> 00:03:24.733
Pollyanna persisted. "Everybody lives somewhere."

38
00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:28.773
"I'm hunting for a new place."

39
00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:32.494
"Oh! Where is it?"

40
00:03:32.495 --> 00:03:36.514
"If I knew where it was, I wouldn't be hunting for it."

41
00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:39.429
Jimmy's voice dripped with scorn.

42
00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:45.530
This was not a nice boy, but he was a young person, so Pollyanna tried again.

43
00:03:45.531 --> 00:03:48.764
"Where did you live before?" she asked.

44
00:03:48.765 --> 00:03:55.665
Jimmy shook his head in disbelief. "Do you always ask so many questions?"

45
00:03:55.666 --> 00:04:01.253
"If you'd talk more, I wouldn't have to pester you with questions."

46
00:04:01.254 --> 00:04:05.914
"Okay!" Jimmy smiled slightly.

47
00:04:05.915 --> 00:04:10.996
"I'm ten, almost eleven, and I went to live at the Orphans' Home last year.

48
00:04:10.997 --> 00:04:14.680
It's so crowded that I left this morning to find a real home.

49
00:04:14.681 --> 00:04:20.474
If you have a home, you have a family, and I haven't had one since—"

50
00:04:20.475 --> 00:04:24.080
Jimmy sniffed as if trying to hold back tears.

51
00:04:24.081 --> 00:04:32.716
"Since Dad died. I tried four houses, but nobody wanted me, even though I volunteered to work.

52
00:04:32.717 --> 00:04:36.288
Is that enough information for you?"

53
00:04:36.289 --> 00:04:40.216
"I know just how you feel," Pollyanna said.

54
00:04:40.217 --> 00:04:48.131
"After my father died, there was nobody to take me in until Aunt Polly—" She stopped and her face lit up.

55
00:04:48.132 --> 00:04:52.671
"Oh! Aunt Polly will be glad to give you a home!

56
00:04:52.672 --> 00:04:59.679
Besides me, she's taken in Fluffy and Buffy, and they're only a cat and a dog."

57
00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:05.473
Jimmy's face brightened. "Would she really?"

58
00:05:05.474 --> 00:05:10.527
"She's so good and kind, the nicest lady in the world!"

59
00:05:10.528 --> 00:05:15.787
Pollyanna jumped up and started running home.

60
00:05:15.788 --> 00:05:21.594
"There's tons of space in her house, though you may have to start out in the attic room.

61
00:05:21.595 --> 00:05:28.767
But it's even nicer now with window screens."

62
00:05:28.768 --> 00:05:31.450
Jimmy laughed as they ran together.

63
00:05:31.451 --> 00:05:35.320
"I never met anyone who talked so much!"

64
00:05:35.321 --> 00:05:39.096
"You should be glad I do," Pollyanna said.

65
00:05:39.097 --> 00:05:45.937
"Because when I'm talking, you don't have to!"

